\f0\b\fs34 \cf2 References and Scientific Basis
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\
(All calculations and recommendations in this framework are grounded in established nutritional science. Key references include: the Mifflin-St Jeor equation for RMR , which is widely validated; the Cunningham/Katch-McArdle formulas for lean-mass-based RMR ; standard PAL multipliers for activity ; the thermic effect of food ~10% assumption  and macronutrient-specific TEF values ; Acceptable Macronutrient Distribution Ranges  from the Institute of Medicine; high-protein diet guidelines for athletes and weight management ; specialized needs for older adults ; and diet-specific macro ratios, such as ketogenic percentages  and paleo diet composition . The weight loss and gain adjustments rely on classic principles of roughly 3500 kcal per pound of fat, hence the 500 kcal/day deficit or surplus rule of thumb  . All these sources underpin the logic, ensuring the calculator\'92s output is not only personalized but also evidence-based and safe.)}